---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ComingSoon from '../components/ComingSoon.astro';
import { PAUSED, CONTACT_EMAIL as CONTACT } from '../config';

const updated = 'October 6, 2026';
---

{PAUSED && (
  <Layout
    title="Spyke Automation"
    description="Something exciting is coming soon."
    noindex
  >
    <ComingSoon />
  </Layout>
)}

{!PAUSED && (
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Spyke Automation"
  description="How Spyke Automation collects, uses, and protects information from visitors to spykeautomation.com."
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="legal" id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p class="lead">
        This policy explains what information Spyke Automation ("we", "us") collects through
        <strong>spykeautomation.com</strong>, why we collect it, and the choices you have. We keep
        data collection to the minimum needed to run an early-access program and improve the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Information you give us.</strong> When you request early access, we collect the
          email address you submit. If you email us, we keep your message and contact details so we
          can reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Usage data.</strong> We use PostHog, hosted in the United States, to understand how
          the site is used: the pages you view, the site that referred you, your device and browser,
          and what you click.
          <ul>
            <li>
              <strong>By default</strong>, PostHog sets a cookie so return visits are recognised,
              keeps a profile of your visits, and records them as session replays, including
              mouse movement, clicks, scrolling and anything typed into the site. It also records
              how fast pages load for you and builds heatmaps of where visitors click and how far
              they scroll. Your approximate location is worked out from your IP address; the IP
              address itself isn't stored.
            </li>
            <li>
              If you choose <strong>Reject all</strong> in the cookie banner, the cookie is deleted
              and session replay stops. Visits are still counted, but with no cookies and nothing
              stored on your device to identify you. Each visit is tied to an identifier that
              changes daily, and your IP address isn't kept.
            </li>
          </ul>
          You can change your answer at any time with "Cookie settings" at the bottom of every page.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting.</strong> Our host, GitHub Pages, may record standard technical
          information such as your IP address and browser type to deliver and secure the site.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookies and similar storage</h2>
      <p>
        Unless you reject analytics, PostHog sets a cookie named
        <code>ph_&lt;project key&gt;_posthog</code>, which lasts 365 days and is shared across
        spykeautomation.com and its subdomains, along with related entries starting with
        <code>ph_</code> in your browser's local and session storage. Whichever answer you give in the
        cookie banner, entries in local storage remember it, so we don't ask again. We use no advertising cookies.
      </p>

      <h2>How we use information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To contact you about early access and product availability.</li>
        <li>To respond to your questions and support requests.</li>
        <li>To operate, secure, and improve the website.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we share information</h2>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal information. We share it only with service
        providers that help us run the site and our early-access program (for example, form,
        email, and hosting providers, PostHog for analytics, and Cloudflare, which carries
        analytics traffic to PostHog), and only as needed to provide
        those services. We may also
        disclose information if required by law.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We keep early-access emails until you ask us to remove them or until we no longer need them
        for the program. You can request deletion at any time using the contact details below.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask us to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you, or
        to stop contacting you, by emailing <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>. Any
        product update emails will also include a way to opt out.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy as the product evolves. When we do, we will revise the "Last
        updated" date above. Material changes will be highlighted on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
)}
